-- ============================================================================
-- P1-seat-subject.l4 -- THE SEAT LAYER OF P1: A DATA SUBJECT.  Articles 2, 4 (points 1, 2, 7, 8) and 5 to 11; there is no Article 24 question in this seat, and no question on point 6 (filing system).
-- Written by P1 (Sonnet 5.5).  Every question calls a layer-1 rule and restates none.
--
-- SEAT: a data subject: a natural person whose personal data are processed.  A child is a data subject: Article 8 is asked from the child as well as from the controller.
-- Questions are phrased `Under Article N, as a data subject, ...`, grouped under § headings in the text's order.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS.  Each input is a yes or no, a number, a date or a choice from a list, with an @desc.  Where a layer-1 rule takes a list or a MAYBE, the
-- list or MAYBE is built here from those plain answers (see the helpers below).  "Not sure" is offered only where a layer-1 rule combines several
-- answers (Article 6(1), 9(2)); it becomes NOTHING and the combining rule answers NOTHING unless another answer already decides it.
-- Borrowed facts (consent, child, necessity, "lawfully", "fairly") are asked as plain facts: PLAN.md section 6.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Regulation itself gives in its own words (a definition that "means", an "only if", a flat
-- "shall not", a "where"); NOTHING means the text does not answer on these facts.  Never read NOTHING as no (NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING").
-- A `Duty outcome` answers "the duty does not arise" (a failed gate), "the duty arises and is met" or "the duty arises and is not met".
--
-- THERE IS NO SEAT FOR AN OFFICIAL.  Where a provision addresses only an official or a lawmaker (Art 6(2), 6(3), 8(1) second subparagraph, 9(4)), the question asks what it means to the data subject.
-- ============================================================================

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Helpers that build the layer-1 inputs from the plain answers.  They only translate; they restate no rule.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- A yes, a no, or "I am not sure", which becomes NOTHING.
DECLARE `P1 subject answer` IS ONE OF
    `P1 subject answer: yes`
    `P1 subject answer: no`
    `P1 subject answer: not sure`

GIVEN answer IS A `P1 subject answer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`P1 subject answer as a yes or no` MEANS
    CONSIDER answer
    WHEN `P1 subject answer: yes` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `P1 subject answer: no` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `P1 subject answer: not sure` THEN NOTHING

GIVEN `the person can be identified` IS A BOOLEAN
      means IS AN `Art 4(1) means of identification`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Art 4(1) means of identification`
`P1 subject ways of identification` MEANS
    IF `the person can be identified` THEN LIST means ELSE EMPTY

GIVEN `a Member State has provided an age` IS A BOOLEAN
      age IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`P1 subject age a Member State has provided` MEANS
    IF `a Member State has provided an age` THEN JUST age ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A BOOLEAN
      e IS A BOOLEAN
      f IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Art 5 principle`
`P1 subject principles shown` MEANS
    (append (IF a THEN LIST `Art 5(1)(a) lawfulness, fairness and transparency` ELSE EMPTY) (append (IF b THEN LIST `Art 5(1)(b) purpose limitation` ELSE EMPTY) (append (IF c THEN LIST `Art 5(1)(c) data minimisation` ELSE EMPTY) (append (IF d THEN LIST `Art 5(1)(d) accuracy` ELSE EMPTY) (append (IF e THEN LIST `Art 5(1)(e) storage limitation` ELSE EMPTY) (IF f THEN LIST `Art 5(1)(f) integrity and confidentiality` ELSE EMPTY))))))

-- (A data subject has no question on Article 6(4) or Article 24, so the helpers that build their matter lists are not needed here; the controller's seat has them.)

§ `Regulation (EU) 2016/679, Articles 2 to 11 -- my questions as a data subject`


§§ `Article 2 -- does the Regulation reach the processing?`

@export Under Article 2(1) and (2), as a data subject, is the processing of my personal data within the material scope of this Regulation?
GIVEN `the operations are processing of personal data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the operations are processing of personal data? Answer true or false.
      `the processing is wholly or partly by automated means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the processing is wholly or partly by automated means? Answer true or false.
      `the personal data form part of a filing system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the personal data form part of a filing system? Answer true or false.
      `the personal data are intended to form part of a filing system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the personal data are intended to form part of a filing system? Answer true or false.
      `the processing is in the course of an activity which falls outside the scope of Union law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the processing is in the course of an activity which falls outside the scope of Union law? Answer true or false.
      `the processing is by a Member State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the processing is by a Member State? Answer true or false.
      `the Member State is carrying out activities which fall within the scope of Chapter 2 of Title V of the TEU` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the Member State is carrying out activities which fall within the scope of Chapter 2 of Title V of the TEU? Answer true or false.
      `the processing is by a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the processing is by a natural person? Answer true or false.
      `the natural person processes in the course of a purely personal or household activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the natural person processes in the course of a purely personal or household activity? Answer true or false.
      `the processing is by a competent authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the processing is by a competent authority? Answer true or false.
      `the purpose of the processing` IS A `Art 2(2)(d) purpose of the processing` @desc The purpose of the processing: choose exactly one of: Art 2(2)(d) prevention of criminal offences; Art 2(2)(d) investigation of criminal offences; Art 2(2)(d) detection of criminal offences; Art 2(2)(d) prosecution of criminal offences; Art 2(2)(d) execution of criminal penalties; Art 2(2)(d) safeguarding against threats to public security; Art 2(2)(d) prevention of threats to public security; Art 2(2)(d) another purpose.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 2(1) and (2), as a data subject, is the processing of my personal data within the material scope of this Regulation` IS
    `Art 2(1) and (2) the processing is within the material scope of this Regulation` (`Art 2(1) this Regulation applies to the processing of personal data` `the operations are processing of personal data` `the processing is wholly or partly by automated means` `the personal data form part of a filing system` `the personal data are intended to form part of a filing system`) (`Art 2(2) this Regulation applies to the processing of personal data, given points (a) to (d)` (`Art 2(2)(a) this Regulation applies to processing in the course of an activity outside the scope of Union law` `the processing is in the course of an activity which falls outside the scope of Union law`) (`Art 2(2)(b) this Regulation applies to processing by the Member States in activities within Chapter 2 of Title V of the TEU` `the processing is by a Member State` `the Member State is carrying out activities which fall within the scope of Chapter 2 of Title V of the TEU`) (`Art 2(2)(c) this Regulation applies to processing by a natural person in the course of a purely personal or household activity` `the processing is by a natural person` `the natural person processes in the course of a purely personal or household activity`) (`Art 2(2)(d) this Regulation applies to processing by competent authorities for the purposes of criminal justice and public security` `the processing is by a competent authority` `the purpose of the processing`))


§§ `Article 4 -- who and what the definitions pick out`

@export Under Article 4(1), as a data subject, is the information about me personal data?
GIVEN `the information relates to a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the information relates to a natural person? Answer true or false.
      `the natural person is identified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the natural person is identified? Answer true or false.
      `the natural person can be identified directly or indirectly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the natural person can be identified directly or indirectly? Answer true or false.
      `how the natural person can be identified` IS A `Art 4(1) means of identification` @desc How the natural person can be identified: choose exactly one of: Art 4(1) a name; Art 4(1) an identification number; Art 4(1) location data; Art 4(1) an online identifier; Art 4(1) a factor specific to the physical identity; Art 4(1) a factor specific to the physiological identity; Art 4(1) a factor specific to the genetic identity; Art 4(1) a factor specific to the mental identity; Art 4(1) a factor specific to the economic identity; Art 4(1) a factor specific to the cultural identity; Art 4(1) a factor specific to the social identity; Art 4(1) some other means of identification.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 4(1), as a data subject, is the information about me personal data` IS
    `Art 4(1) the information is personal data` `the information relates to a natural person` `the natural person is identified` (`P1 subject ways of identification` `the natural person can be identified directly or indirectly` `how the natural person can be identified`)

@export Under Article 4(1), as a data subject, am I a data subject in relation to this information?
GIVEN `I am a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that I am a natural person? Answer true or false.
      `the information relates to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the information relates to me? Answer true or false.
      `I am identified by the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that I am identified by the information? Answer true or false.
      `I can be identified directly or indirectly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that I can be identified directly or indirectly? Answer true or false.
      `how I can be identified` IS A `Art 4(1) means of identification` @desc How I can be identified: choose exactly one of: Art 4(1) a name; Art 4(1) an identification number; Art 4(1) location data; Art 4(1) an online identifier; Art 4(1) a factor specific to the physical identity; Art 4(1) a factor specific to the physiological identity; Art 4(1) a factor specific to the genetic identity; Art 4(1) a factor specific to the mental identity; Art 4(1) a factor specific to the economic identity; Art 4(1) a factor specific to the cultural identity; Art 4(1) a factor specific to the social identity; Art 4(1) some other means of identification.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 4(1), as a data subject, am I a data subject in relation to this information` IS
    `Art 4(1) the person is a data subject` `I am a natural person` `the information relates to me` `I am identified by the information` (`P1 subject ways of identification` `I can be identified directly or indirectly` `how I can be identified`)

@export Under Article 4(2), as a data subject, is what was done with my personal data processing?
GIVEN `what is done with the personal data` IS A `Art 4(2) operation on personal data` @desc What is done with the personal data: choose exactly one of: Art 4(2) collection; Art 4(2) recording; Art 4(2) organisation; Art 4(2) structuring; Art 4(2) storage; Art 4(2) adaptation; Art 4(2) alteration; Art 4(2) retrieval; Art 4(2) consultation; Art 4(2) use; Art 4(2) disclosure by transmission; Art 4(2) dissemination; Art 4(2) otherwise making available; Art 4(2) alignment; Art 4(2) combination; Art 4(2) restriction; Art 4(2) erasure; Art 4(2) destruction; Art 4(2) some other operation.
      `the operations are performed on personal data or on sets of personal data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the operations are performed on personal data or on sets of personal data? Answer true or false.
      `the operations are performed by automated means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the operations are performed by automated means? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 4(2), as a data subject, is what was done with my personal data processing` IS
    `Art 4(2) the operations are processing` (LIST `what is done with the personal data`) `the operations are performed on personal data or on sets of personal data` `the operations are performed by automated means`

@export Under Article 4(7), as a data subject, is a body that decides why and how my personal data are processed a controller?
GIVEN `the kind of body` IS A `Kind of person or body` @desc The kind of body: choose exactly one of: natural person; legal person; public authority; agency; other body; not a person or body.
      `the body decides the purposes of the processing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the body decides the purposes of the processing? Answer true or false.
      `the body decides the means of the processing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the body decides the means of the processing? Answer true or false.
      `Union or Member State law determines the purposes and means of the processing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that Union or Member State law determines the purposes and means of the processing? Answer true or false.
      `that law provides for the body as the controller, or sets criteria for nominating the controller that the body meets` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that that law provides for the body as the controller, or sets criteria for nominating the controller that the body meets? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 4(7), as a data subject, is a body that decides why and how my personal data are processed a controller` IS
    `Art 4(7) the body is a controller` `the kind of body` `the body decides the purposes of the processing` `the body decides the means of the processing` `Union or Member State law determines the purposes and means of the processing` `that law provides for the body as the controller, or sets criteria for nominating the controller that the body meets`

@export Under Article 4(7), as a data subject, is a controller that decides why and how my personal data are processed deciding alone or jointly with others?
GIVEN `the body decides the purposes of the processing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the body decides the purposes of the processing? Answer true or false.
      `the body decides the means of the processing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the body decides the means of the processing? Answer true or false.
      `the body decides them jointly with another body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the body decides them jointly with another body? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE `Art 4(7) how a controller determines the purposes and means`
DECIDE `Under Article 4(7), as a data subject, is a controller that decides why and how my personal data are processed deciding alone or jointly with others` IS
    `Art 4(7) how the body determines the purposes and means` `the body decides the purposes of the processing` `the body decides the means of the processing` `the body decides them jointly with another body`

@export Under Article 4(8), as a data subject, is the body that processes my personal data on behalf of another a processor?
GIVEN `the kind of body` IS A `Kind of person or body` @desc The kind of body: choose exactly one of: natural person; legal person; public authority; agency; other body; not a person or body.
      `the body processes personal data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the body processes personal data? Answer true or false.
      `the body processes it on behalf of the controller` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the body processes it on behalf of the controller? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 4(8), as a data subject, is the body that processes my personal data on behalf of another a processor` IS
    `Art 4(8) the body is a processor` `the kind of body` `the body processes personal data` `the body processes it on behalf of the controller`


§§ `Article 5 -- the principles the processing must meet`

@export Under Article 5(1)(a), as a data subject, are my personal data processed lawfully, fairly and in a transparent manner?
GIVEN `the personal data are processed lawfully` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the personal data are processed lawfully? Answer true or false.
      `the personal data are processed fairly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the personal data are processed fairly? Answer true or false.
      `the personal data are processed in a transparent manner in relation to the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the personal data are processed in a transparent manner in relation to the data subject? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 5(1)(a), as a data subject, are my personal data processed lawfully, fairly and in a transparent manner` IS
    `Art 5(1)(a) the personal data are processed lawfully, fairly and in a transparent manner in relation to the data subject` `the personal data are processed lawfully` `the personal data are processed fairly` `the personal data are processed in a transparent manner in relation to the data subject`

@export Under Article 5(1)(c), as a data subject, are the personal data processed about me adequate, relevant and limited to what is necessary?
GIVEN `the personal data are adequate in relation to the purposes for which they are processed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the personal data are adequate in relation to the purposes for which they are processed? Answer true or false.
      `the personal data are relevant in relation to the purposes for which they are processed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the personal data are relevant in relation to the purposes for which they are processed? Answer true or false.
      `the personal data are limited to what is necessary in relation to the purposes for which they are processed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the personal data are limited to what is necessary in relation to the purposes for which they are processed? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 5(1)(c), as a data subject, are the personal data processed about me adequate, relevant and limited to what is necessary` IS
    `Art 5(1)(c) the personal data are adequate, relevant and limited to what is necessary in relation to the purposes for which they are processed` `the personal data are adequate in relation to the purposes for which they are processed` `the personal data are relevant in relation to the purposes for which they are processed` `the personal data are limited to what is necessary in relation to the purposes for which they are processed`

@export Under Article 5(1)(d), as a data subject, are the personal data processed about me accurate and, where necessary, kept up to date?
GIVEN `the personal data are accurate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the personal data are accurate? Answer true or false.
      `keeping the personal data up to date is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that keeping the personal data up to date is necessary? Answer true or false.
      `the personal data are kept up to date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the personal data are kept up to date? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 5(1)(d), as a data subject, are the personal data processed about me accurate and, where necessary, kept up to date` IS
    `Art 5(1)(d) the personal data are accurate and, where necessary, kept up to date` `the personal data are accurate` `keeping the personal data up to date is necessary` `the personal data are kept up to date`

@export Under Article 5(1)(d), as a data subject, has every reasonable step been taken to erase or rectify inaccurate personal data about me without delay?
GIVEN `some of the personal data are inaccurate, having regard to the purposes for which they are processed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that some of the personal data are inaccurate, having regard to the purposes for which they are processed? Answer true or false.
      `every reasonable step has been taken to erase or rectify the inaccurate personal data without delay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that every reasonable step has been taken to erase or rectify the inaccurate personal data without delay? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE `Duty outcome`
DECIDE `Under Article 5(1)(d), as a data subject, has every reasonable step been taken to erase or rectify inaccurate personal data about me without delay` IS
    `Art 5(1)(d) every reasonable step is taken to ensure that inaccurate personal data are erased or rectified without delay` `some of the personal data are inaccurate, having regard to the purposes for which they are processed` `every reasonable step has been taken to erase or rectify the inaccurate personal data without delay`

@export Under Article 5(1)(e), as a data subject, are the personal data about me kept in a form which permits my identification no longer than is necessary?
GIVEN `the personal data are kept in a form which permits identification of data subjects` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the personal data are kept in a form which permits identification of data subjects? Answer true or false.
      `they are kept for longer than is necessary for the purposes for which they are processed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that they are kept for longer than is necessary for the purposes for which they are processed? Answer true or false.
      `the personal data will be processed solely for` IS A `Art 5(1)(b) purpose of archiving, research or statistics` @desc The personal data will be processed solely for: choose exactly one of: Art 5(1)(b) archiving purposes in the public interest; Art 5(1)(b) scientific research purposes; Art 5(1)(b) historical research purposes; Art 5(1)(b) statistical purposes; Art 5(1)(b) some other purpose.
      `the processing is in accordance with Article 89(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the processing is in accordance with Article 89(1)? Answer true or false.
      `the appropriate technical and organisational measures required by this Regulation are implemented to safeguard the rights and freedoms of the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the appropriate technical and organisational measures required by this Regulation are implemented to safeguard the rights and freedoms of the data subject? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 5(1)(e), as a data subject, are the personal data about me kept in a form which permits my identification no longer than is necessary` IS
    `Art 5(1)(e) the personal data are kept in a form which permits identification of data subjects for no longer than is necessary for the purposes for which they are processed` `the personal data are kept in a form which permits identification of data subjects` `they are kept for longer than is necessary for the purposes for which they are processed` (`Art 5(1)(e) the personal data may be stored for longer periods` `the personal data will be processed solely for` `the processing is in accordance with Article 89(1)` `the appropriate technical and organisational measures required by this Regulation are implemented to safeguard the rights and freedoms of the data subject`)

@export Under Article 5(2), as a data subject, is the controller able to demonstrate compliance with Article 5(1)?
GIVEN `the controller can demonstrate lawfulness, fairness and transparency (Art 5(1)(a))` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, can the controller demonstrate compliance with 5(1)(a? Answer true or false.
      `the controller can demonstrate purpose limitation (Art 5(1)(b))` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, can the controller demonstrate compliance with 5(1)(b? Answer true or false.
      `the controller can demonstrate data minimisation (Art 5(1)(c))` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, can the controller demonstrate compliance with 5(1)(c? Answer true or false.
      `the controller can demonstrate accuracy (Art 5(1)(d))` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, can the controller demonstrate compliance with 5(1)(d? Answer true or false.
      `the controller can demonstrate storage limitation (Art 5(1)(e))` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, can the controller demonstrate compliance with 5(1)(e? Answer true or false.
      `the controller can demonstrate integrity and confidentiality (Art 5(1)(f))` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, can the controller demonstrate compliance with 5(1)(f? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 5(2), as a data subject, is the controller able to demonstrate compliance with Article 5(1)` IS
    `Art 5(2) the controller is able to demonstrate compliance with Art 5(1)` (`P1 subject principles shown` `the controller can demonstrate lawfulness, fairness and transparency (Art 5(1)(a))` `the controller can demonstrate purpose limitation (Art 5(1)(b))` `the controller can demonstrate data minimisation (Art 5(1)(c))` `the controller can demonstrate accuracy (Art 5(1)(d))` `the controller can demonstrate storage limitation (Art 5(1)(e))` `the controller can demonstrate integrity and confidentiality (Art 5(1)(f))`)


§§ `Article 6 -- a lawful basis for the processing`

@export Under Article 6(1)(a), as a data subject, have I consented to the processing of my personal data for one or more specific purposes?
GIVEN `the data subject has given consent to the processing of his or her personal data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the data subject has given consent to the processing of his or her personal data? Answer true or false.
      `the consent is for one or more specific purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the consent is for one or more specific purposes? Answer true or false.
      `the processing is for one of those purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the processing is for one of those purposes? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 6(1)(a), as a data subject, have I consented to the processing of my personal data for one or more specific purposes` IS
    `Art 6(1)(a) point (a) applies: the data subject has given consent to the processing for one or more specific purposes` `the data subject has given consent to the processing of his or her personal data` `the consent is for one or more specific purposes` `the processing is for one of those purposes`

@export Under Article 6(1)(b), as a data subject, is the processing necessary for a contract to which I am party or for steps I asked for before one?
GIVEN `the processing is necessary for the performance of a contract to which the data subject is party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the processing is necessary for the performance of a contract to which the data subject is party? Answer true or false.
      `the processing is necessary in order to take steps at the request of the data subject prior to entering into a contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the processing is necessary in order to take steps at the request of the data subject prior to entering into a contract? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 6(1)(b), as a data subject, is the processing necessary for a contract to which I am party or for steps I asked for before one` IS
    `Art 6(1)(b) point (b) applies: the processing is necessary for a contract with the data subject or for steps before one` `the processing is necessary for the performance of a contract to which the data subject is party` `the processing is necessary in order to take steps at the request of the data subject prior to entering into a contract`

@export Under Article 6(1)(f), as a data subject, does point (f) (legitimate interests) apply to the processing of my personal data?
GIVEN `the processing is necessary for the purposes of the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the processing is necessary for the purposes of the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party? Answer true or false.
      `those interests are overridden by the interests or fundamental rights and freedoms of the data subject which require protection of personal data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that those interests are overridden by the interests or fundamental rights and freedoms of the data subject which require protection of personal data? Answer true or false.
      `the data subject is a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the data subject is a child? Answer true or false.
      `the processing is carried out by a public authority in the performance of its tasks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the processing is carried out by a public authority in the performance of its tasks? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 6(1)(f), as a data subject, does point (f) (legitimate interests) apply to the processing of my personal data` IS
    `Art 6(1)(f) point (f) applies: the processing is necessary for legitimate interests that are not overridden` `the processing is necessary for the purposes of the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party` `those interests are overridden by the interests or fundamental rights and freedoms of the data subject which require protection of personal data` `the data subject is a child` `the processing is carried out by a public authority in the performance of its tasks`


§§ `Article 7 -- consent`

@export Under Article 7(1), as a data subject, is the controller able to demonstrate that I have consented?
GIVEN `the processing is based on consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the processing is based on consent? Answer true or false.
      `the controller is able to demonstrate that the data subject has consented to processing of his or her personal data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the controller is able to demonstrate that the data subject has consented to processing of his or her personal data? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE `Duty outcome`
DECIDE `Under Article 7(1), as a data subject, is the controller able to demonstrate that I have consented` IS
    `Art 7(1) the controller is able to demonstrate that the data subject has consented` `the processing is based on consent` `the controller is able to demonstrate that the data subject has consented to processing of his or her personal data`

@export Under Article 7(2), as a data subject, is the request for my consent presented clearly where my consent is given in a written declaration that also concerns other matters?
GIVEN `consent is given in the context of a written declaration which also concerns other matters` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that consent is given in the context of a written declaration which also concerns other matters? Answer true or false.
      `the request for consent is presented in a manner which is clearly distinguishable from the other matters` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the request for consent is presented in a manner which is clearly distinguishable from the other matters? Answer true or false.
      `the request is in an intelligible and easily accessible form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the request is in an intelligible and easily accessible form? Answer true or false.
      `the request uses clear and plain language` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the request uses clear and plain language? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE `Duty outcome`
DECIDE `Under Article 7(2), as a data subject, is the request for my consent presented clearly where my consent is given in a written declaration that also concerns other matters` IS
    `Art 7(2) the request for consent is presented clearly where consent is given in a written declaration that also concerns other matters` `consent is given in the context of a written declaration which also concerns other matters` `the request for consent is presented in a manner which is clearly distinguishable from the other matters` `the request is in an intelligible and easily accessible form` `the request uses clear and plain language`

@export Under Article 7(2), as a data subject, is a part of a declaration I gave that infringes this Regulation binding on me?
GIVEN `the part is part of such a declaration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the part is part of such a declaration? Answer true or false.
      `the part constitutes an infringement of this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the part constitutes an infringement of this Regulation? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 7(2), as a data subject, is a part of a declaration I gave that infringes this Regulation binding on me` IS
    `Art 7(2) the part of the declaration is binding` `the part is part of such a declaration` `the part constitutes an infringement of this Regulation`

@export Under Article 7(3), as a data subject, may I withdraw my consent at any time?
GIVEN `the data subject has given consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the data subject has given consent? Answer true or false.
      `the day on which consent was given` IS A DATE @desc On what date: the day on which consent was given?
      `the day on which the data subject withdraws it` IS A DATE @desc On what date: the day on which the data subject withdraws it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 7(3), as a data subject, may I withdraw my consent at any time` IS
    `Art 7(3) the data subject may withdraw his or her consent at any time` `the data subject has given consent` `the day on which consent was given` `the day on which the data subject withdraws it`

@export Under Article 7(3), as a data subject, does my withdrawal of consent affect the lawfulness of the processing before it?
GIVEN `the processing was based on consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the processing was based on consent? Answer true or false.
      `the processing took place before the withdrawal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the processing took place before the withdrawal? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 7(3), as a data subject, does my withdrawal of consent affect the lawfulness of the processing before it` IS
    `Art 7(3) the withdrawal of consent affects the lawfulness of the processing` `the processing was based on consent` `the processing took place before the withdrawal`

@export Under Article 7(3), as a data subject, was I informed of the right to withdraw consent before I gave consent?
GIVEN `the data subject has given consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the data subject has given consent? Answer true or false.
      `the data subject was informed of the right to withdraw consent before giving consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the data subject was informed of the right to withdraw consent before giving consent? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 7(3), as a data subject, was I informed of the right to withdraw consent before I gave consent` IS
    `Art 7(3) the data subject was informed of the right to withdraw consent prior to giving consent` `the data subject has given consent` `the data subject was informed of the right to withdraw consent before giving consent`

@export Under Article 7(3), as a data subject, is it as easy for me to withdraw consent as to give it?
GIVEN `withdrawing consent is as easy as giving consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that withdrawing consent is as easy as giving consent? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 7(3), as a data subject, is it as easy for me to withdraw consent as to give it` IS
    `Art 7(3) it is as easy to withdraw consent as to give it` `withdrawing consent is as easy as giving consent`

@export Under Article 7(4), as a data subject, is the conditionality of the contract on my consent a matter of which utmost account is taken in assessing whether my consent is freely given?
GIVEN `consent is being assessed for whether it is freely given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that consent is being assessed for whether it is freely given? Answer true or false.
      `the performance of a contract, including the provision of a service, is conditional on consent to the processing of personal data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the performance of a contract, including the provision of a service, is conditional on consent to the processing of personal data? Answer true or false.
      `that processing is necessary for the performance of that contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that that processing is necessary for the performance of that contract? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 7(4), as a data subject, is the conditionality of the contract on my consent a matter of which utmost account is taken in assessing whether my consent is freely given` IS
    `Art 7(4) the conditionality of the contract on consent that is not necessary for it is a matter of which utmost account is taken` `consent is being assessed for whether it is freely given` `the performance of a contract, including the provision of a service, is conditional on consent to the processing of personal data` `that processing is necessary for the performance of that contract`


§§ `Article 8 -- a child's consent to information society services`

@export Under Article 8(1), as a data subject, does the processing of my personal data as a child meet the condition of Article 8(1)?
GIVEN `point (a) of Article 6(1) applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that point (a) of Article 6(1) applies? Answer true or false.
      `the information society services are offered directly to a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the information society services are offered directly to a child? Answer true or false.
      `the age of the child in complete years` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the age of the child in complete years? Give a number.
      `a Member State has provided by law for a lower age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that a Member State has provided by law for a lower age? Answer true or false.
      `the lower age a Member State has provided by law` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the lower age a Member State has provided by law? Give a number.
      `consent is given or authorised by the holder of parental responsibility over the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that consent is given or authorised by the holder of parental responsibility over the child? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 8(1), as a data subject, does the processing of my personal data as a child meet the condition of Article 8(1)` IS
    `Art 8(1) the processing of a child's personal data meets the condition of Art 8(1)` `point (a) of Article 6(1) applies` `the information society services are offered directly to a child` `the age of the child in complete years` (`P1 subject age a Member State has provided` `a Member State has provided by law for a lower age` `the lower age a Member State has provided by law`) `consent is given or authorised by the holder of parental responsibility over the child`

@export Under Article 8(1), as a data subject, is the consent of my parent or guardian (the holder of parental responsibility) needed for the processing of my personal data?
GIVEN `point (a) of Article 6(1) applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that point (a) of Article 6(1) applies? Answer true or false.
      `the information society services are offered directly to a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the information society services are offered directly to a child? Answer true or false.
      `the age of the child in complete years` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the age of the child in complete years? Give a number.
      `a Member State has provided by law for a lower age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that a Member State has provided by law for a lower age? Answer true or false.
      `the lower age a Member State has provided by law` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the lower age a Member State has provided by law? Give a number.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 8(1), as a data subject, is the consent of my parent or guardian (the holder of parental responsibility) needed for the processing of my personal data` IS
    `Art 8(1) the case is one in which the consent of the holder of parental responsibility is needed` `point (a) of Article 6(1) applies` `the information society services are offered directly to a child` `the age of the child in complete years` (`P1 subject age a Member State has provided` `a Member State has provided by law for a lower age` `the lower age a Member State has provided by law`)

@export Under Article 8(1), as a data subject, from what age may I consent myself in my Member State?
GIVEN `a Member State has provided by law for a lower age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that a Member State has provided by law for a lower age? Answer true or false.
      `the lower age a Member State has provided by law` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the lower age a Member State has provided by law? Give a number.
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Article 8(1), as a data subject, from what age may I consent myself in my Member State` IS
    `Art 8(1) the age from which the child may consent in this Member State` (`P1 subject age a Member State has provided` `a Member State has provided by law for a lower age` `the lower age a Member State has provided by law`)


§§ `Article 9 -- special categories of personal data`

@export Under Article 9(1), as a data subject, are the personal data about me of a category the Regulation names?
GIVEN `the category of the personal data` IS A `Art 9(1) category of personal data` @desc The category of the personal data: choose exactly one of: Art 9(1) data revealing racial or ethnic origin; Art 9(1) data revealing political opinions; Art 9(1) data revealing religious or philosophical beliefs; Art 9(1) data revealing trade union membership; Art 9(1) genetic data; Art 9(1) biometric data for the purpose of uniquely identifying a natural person; Art 9(1) data concerning health; Art 9(1) data concerning a natural person's sex life or sexual orientation; Art 9(1) biometric data not for the purpose of uniquely identifying a natural person; Art 9(1) other personal data.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 9(1), as a data subject, are the personal data about me of a category the Regulation names` IS
    `Art 9(1) the categories processed include one that paragraph 1 names` (LIST `the category of the personal data`)

@export Under Article 9(2)(a), as a data subject, does point (a) (explicit consent) apply to the processing of my personal data?
GIVEN `the data subject has given explicit consent to the processing of those personal data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the data subject has given explicit consent to the processing of those personal data? Answer true or false.
      `the consent is for one or more specified purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the consent is for one or more specified purposes? Answer true or false.
      `Union or Member State law provides that the prohibition referred to in paragraph 1 may not be lifted by the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that Union or Member State law provides that the prohibition referred to in paragraph 1 may not be lifted by the data subject? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 9(2)(a), as a data subject, does point (a) (explicit consent) apply to the processing of my personal data` IS
    `Art 9(2)(a) point (a) applies: the data subject has given explicit consent to the processing for one or more specified purposes` `the data subject has given explicit consent to the processing of those personal data` `the consent is for one or more specified purposes` `Union or Member State law provides that the prohibition referred to in paragraph 1 may not be lifted by the data subject`

@export Under Article 9(2)(c), as a data subject, does point (c) (vital interests where the data subject cannot give consent) apply to the processing of my personal data?
GIVEN `the processing is necessary to protect vital interests` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the processing is necessary to protect vital interests? Answer true or false.
      `whose vital interests` IS A `Art 6(1)(d) whose vital interests` @desc Whose vital interests: choose exactly one of: Art 6(1)(d) the data subject's; Art 6(1)(d) another natural person's; Art 6(1)(d) the interests of something that is not a natural person.
      `the data subject is physically or legally incapable of giving consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the data subject is physically or legally incapable of giving consent? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 9(2)(c), as a data subject, does point (c) (vital interests where the data subject cannot give consent) apply to the processing of my personal data` IS
    `Art 9(2)(c) point (c) applies: the processing is necessary to protect vital interests where the data subject cannot give consent` `the processing is necessary to protect vital interests` `whose vital interests` `the data subject is physically or legally incapable of giving consent`

@export Under Article 9(2)(e), as a data subject, does point (e) (data manifestly made public by the data subject) apply to the processing of my personal data?
GIVEN `the processing relates to personal data which have been made public by the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the processing relates to personal data which have been made public by the data subject? Answer true or false.
      `the data subject made them public manifestly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the data subject made them public manifestly? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 9(2)(e), as a data subject, does point (e) (data manifestly made public by the data subject) apply to the processing of my personal data` IS
    `Art 9(2)(e) point (e) applies: the processing relates to personal data which are manifestly made public by the data subject` `the processing relates to personal data which have been made public by the data subject` `the data subject made them public manifestly`

@export Under Article 9(1) and (2), as a data subject, is the processing of this category of personal data about me prohibited?
GIVEN `the category of the personal data` IS A `Art 9(1) category of personal data` @desc The category of the personal data: choose exactly one of: Art 9(1) data revealing racial or ethnic origin; Art 9(1) data revealing political opinions; Art 9(1) data revealing religious or philosophical beliefs; Art 9(1) data revealing trade union membership; Art 9(1) genetic data; Art 9(1) biometric data for the purpose of uniquely identifying a natural person; Art 9(1) data concerning health; Art 9(1) data concerning a natural person's sex life or sexual orientation; Art 9(1) biometric data not for the purpose of uniquely identifying a natural person; Art 9(1) other personal data.
      `one of points (a) to (j) of Article 9(2) applies` IS A `P1 subject answer` @desc Does one of the ten points of Article 9(2) apply to the processing (for example explicit consent, or data manifestly made public)? Answer P1 subject answer: yes, P1 subject answer: no or P1 subject answer: not sure (not sure is treated as not covered).
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 9(1) and (2), as a data subject, is the processing of this category of personal data about me prohibited` IS
    `Art 9(1) the processing of personal data of a category named in paragraph 1 is prohibited` (LIST `the category of the personal data`) (`P1 subject answer as a yes or no` `one of points (a) to (j) of Article 9(2) applies`)


§§ `Article 10 -- criminal convictions and offences`

@export Under Article 10, as a data subject, does the processing of data about my criminal convictions meet the condition of Article 10?
GIVEN `the personal data relate to criminal convictions and offences or related security measures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the personal data relate to criminal convictions and offences or related security measures? Answer true or false.
      `the processing is based on Article 6(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the processing is based on Article 6(1)? Answer true or false.
      `the processing is carried out under the control of official authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the processing is carried out under the control of official authority? Answer true or false.
      `the processing is authorised by Union or Member State law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the processing is authorised by Union or Member State law? Answer true or false.
      `that law provides for appropriate safeguards for the rights and freedoms of data subjects` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that that law provides for appropriate safeguards for the rights and freedoms of data subjects? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 10, as a data subject, does the processing of data about my criminal convictions meet the condition of Article 10` IS
    `Art 10 the processing of personal data relating to criminal convictions and offences or related security measures meets the condition of Art 10` `the personal data relate to criminal convictions and offences or related security measures` `the processing is based on Article 6(1)` `the processing is carried out under the control of official authority` `the processing is authorised by Union or Member State law` `that law provides for appropriate safeguards for the rights and freedoms of data subjects`

@export Under Article 10, as a data subject, is a comprehensive register of criminal convictions kept only under the control of official authority?
GIVEN `the register is a comprehensive register of criminal convictions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the register is a comprehensive register of criminal convictions? Answer true or false.
      `the register is kept under the control of official authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the register is kept under the control of official authority? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 10, as a data subject, is a comprehensive register of criminal convictions kept only under the control of official authority` IS
    `Art 10 the comprehensive register of criminal convictions is kept only under the control of official authority` `the register is a comprehensive register of criminal convictions` `the register is kept under the control of official authority`


§§ `Article 11 -- processing which does not require identification`

@export Under Article 11(1), as a data subject, is the controller obliged to maintain, acquire or process additional information to identify me?
GIVEN `the purposes for which the controller processes personal data do not or do no longer require the identification of a data subject by the controller` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the purposes for which the controller processes personal data do not or do no longer require the identification of a data subject by the controller? Answer true or false.
      `the additional information would be maintained, acquired or processed for the sole purpose of complying with this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the additional information would be maintained, acquired or processed for the sole purpose of complying with this Regulation? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 11(1), as a data subject, is the controller obliged to maintain, acquire or process additional information to identify me` IS
    `Art 11(1) the controller is obliged to maintain, acquire or process additional information in order to identify the data subject` `the purposes for which the controller processes personal data do not or do no longer require the identification of a data subject by the controller` `the additional information would be maintained, acquired or processed for the sole purpose of complying with this Regulation`

@export Under Article 11(2), as a data subject, must the controller inform me that it is not in a position to identify me, and has it?
GIVEN `the case is one referred to in paragraph 1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the case is one referred to in paragraph 1? Answer true or false.
      `the controller is able to demonstrate that it is not in a position to identify the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the controller is able to demonstrate that it is not in a position to identify the data subject? Answer true or false.
      `it is possible to inform the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that it is possible to inform the data subject? Answer true or false.
      `the controller has informed the data subject accordingly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the controller has informed the data subject accordingly? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE `Duty outcome`
DECIDE `Under Article 11(2), as a data subject, must the controller inform me that it is not in a position to identify me, and has it` IS
    `Art 11(2) the controller informs the data subject that it is not in a position to identify the data subject` `the case is one referred to in paragraph 1` `the controller is able to demonstrate that it is not in a position to identify the data subject` `it is possible to inform the data subject` `the controller has informed the data subject accordingly`

@export Under Article 11(2), as a data subject, are Articles 15 to 20 disapplied for my request?
GIVEN `the case is one referred to in paragraph 1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the case is one referred to in paragraph 1? Answer true or false.
      `the controller is able to demonstrate that it is not in a position to identify the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the controller is able to demonstrate that it is not in a position to identify the data subject? Answer true or false.
      `the data subject, for the purpose of exercising his or her rights under Articles 15 to 20, has provided additional information enabling his or her identification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the data subject, for the purpose of exercising his or her rights under Articles 15 to 20, has provided additional information enabling his or her identification? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 11(2), as a data subject, are Articles 15 to 20 disapplied for my request` IS
    `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` `the case is one referred to in paragraph 1` `the controller is able to demonstrate that it is not in a position to identify the data subject` `the data subject, for the purpose of exercising his or her rights under Articles 15 to 20, has provided additional information enabling his or her identification`
